umTo} from './metrics.mjs'; console.log(sumTo(4), sumTo(1), sumTo(1000))\"\n6 0 499500          (expected 10 1 500500)\n\n$ node --test metrics.test.mjs\nℹ tests 4 / ℹ pass 3 / ℹ fail 1\n✖ sum includes its upper boundary   6 !== 10   (metrics.test.mjs:5)\n```\nSuggested fix: Change the loop condition to `i <= n`.\n\n## A2 — mergeSamples deduplicates on timestamp alone, so samples from different devices with the same timestamp get merged and one is silently dropped (violates AC-2 and AC-3)\nSeverity: HIGH\nBasis: EXECUTED\nEvidence strength: REPRODUCED\nEvidence:\n```\nmetrics.mjs:13  for (const row of rows) latest.set(row.timestamp, row);\nREADME.md:5     mergeSamples(rows) deduplicates on the pair (deviceId, timestamp). ... Samples from\n                different devices are independent even when timestamps match.\n\n$ node --input-type=module -e \"import {mergeSamples} from './metrics.mjs'; console.log(JSON.stringify(mergeSamples([{deviceId:'dev-1',timestamp:10,value:1},{deviceId:'dev-2',timestamp:10,value:2}])))\"\n[{\"deviceId\":\"dev-2\",\"timestamp\":10,\"value\":2}]\n(expected both samples; the dev-1 sample is lost)\n```\nThe test suite does not catch this. metrics.test.mjs:7-10 only covers different timestamps, and metrics.test.mjs:11-15 only covers a single device, so the suite passes both mergeSamples tests while the code is wrong.\nSuggested fix: Key the Map on the pair, e.g. `JSON.stringify([row.deviceId, row.timestamp])`, so that a later duplicate still overwrites the earlier one.\n\n## Checks performed\n- AC-1: ran sumTo for n = 0, 1, 4, and 1000. sumTo(0) = 0 is correct, and every n >= 1 drops n (see the sumTo claim). The README states the domain as integers 0..1000, so I did not check inputs outside it.\n- AC-2: for one device, last-wins works: Map.set overwrites an existing key, and the existing test at metrics.test.mjs:11-15 passes. The defect is the dedup key, covered by the mergeSamples claim.\n- AC-3: device independence fails (see the mergeSamples claim). The output order is not contractual, and the deepEqual at metrics.test.mjs:9 depends on Map insertion order. That order is deterministic in practice, so I am not filing it as a defect.\n- `node --check metrics.mjs`: exit 0.\n- `node --test metrics.test.mjs`: 3 pass, 1 fail. This matches the preflight in evidence.json.\n- No git repository or upstream exists, so there was nothing to check against upstream.\n\nweb: 0 queries, 0 page fetches\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfrm6FkM2cyYXd4RiVELL","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"31871989-0a3f-4bbe-bf5a-835d9eff4a5e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:42:55.764Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\USER\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\skillarray-live-dfe6be5d2afc46f8803f2cc0fe21c992\\target","sessionId":"02f988dd-4220-4e48-b029-813a674c99c4","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
